---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import Figure from '../components/Figure.astro';
import Calc from '../components/Calc.astro';
const faq = [
 {
  "q": "What is the 8th Pay Commission salary at Level 11?",
  "a": "It has not been announced. Level 11 entry basic pay is Rs 67,700 today. Illustrative scenarios give Rs 1,30,000 at 1.92, Rs 1,54,400 at 2.28, Rs 1,74,000 at 2.57 and Rs 1,93,600 at 2.86. These are multiples, not government figures."
 },
 {
  "q": "What is the in-hand salary at Level 11 today?",
  "a": "At the entry cell in a Class X city, gross pay is about Rs 1,36,529 and in-hand pay is about Rs 1,25,494 after a 10% NPS or UPS contribution, before CGHS, CGEGIS and tax. Your payslip is the final authority."
 },
 {
  "q": "Will DA be added to my Level 11 basic pay?",
  "a": "That has not been decided. Past commissions absorbed DA through the fitment factor. If that happens again, a factor of 1.63 would only match today's basic plus DA of Rs 1,10,351, so the real gain at Level 11 is the factor minus 1.63 as a share of 1.63."
 }
];
const toc = [{"id": "today", "label": "Level 11 pay today (7th CPC)"}, {"id": "scenarios", "label": "Level 11 salary under 8th CPC scenarios"}, {"id": "progression", "label": "Level 11 pay matrix: first 10 cells"}, {"id": "promotion", "label": "What promotion or MACP is worth at Level 11"}, {"id": "estimate", "label": "Estimate your own Level 11 salary under the 8th CPC"}, {"id": "faq", "label": "FAQ"}];
const related = ["8th-pay-commission-salary-calculator", "8th-pay-commission-pay-matrix", "fitment-factor-8th-pay-commission", "8th-pay-commission-level-10-salary"];
---

<SiteLayout title="8th Pay Commission Level 11 Salary: Pay Matrix and Estimates" description="Level 11 basic pay is Rs 67,700 today. See 8th Pay Commission Level 11 salary at 1.92, 2.28, 2.57 and 2.86 fitment, with cells, DA, HRA and promotion pay." slug="8th-pay-commission-level-11-salary" h1="8th Pay Commission Level 11 Salary" lead="Level 11 pay today, the first 10 matrix cells, scenario pay and what promotion is worth." faq={faq} toc={toc} related={related} pageType="article" breadcrumbLabel="Level 11 Salary">

<div class="answer"><p><strong>Short answer:</strong> Level 11 entry basic pay is Rs 67,700 a month under the 7th CPC, or Rs 1,10,351 with DA at 63%. The 8th CPC has not announced a fitment factor. At illustrative factors of 1.92 to 2.86, entry basic would be Rs 1,30,000 to Rs 1,93,600.</p></div>

<h2 id="today">Level 11 pay today (7th CPC)</h2>
<p>Level 11 is used for Group A officers in the senior time scale. The entry cell is Rs 67,700 a month. The table below adds DA at 63% (from 1 July 2026), HRA at the current 30 / 20 / 10 rates and Transport Allowance with DA (base slab for a city that is not in the higher-TPTA list).</p><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Component</th><th class="num">Class X city</th><th class="num">Class Y city</th><th class="num">Class Z city</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Basic pay (entry cell)</th><td class="num">₹67,700</td><td class="num">₹67,700</td><td class="num">₹67,700</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Dearness Allowance (63%)</th><td class="num">₹42,651</td><td class="num">₹42,651</td><td class="num">₹42,651</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">HRA (30% / 20% / 10%)</th><td class="num">₹20,310</td><td class="num">₹13,540</td><td class="num">₹6,770</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Transport Allowance with DA</th><td class="num">₹5,868</td><td class="num">₹5,868</td><td class="num">₹5,868</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><strong>Gross monthly pay</strong></th><td class="num">₹1,36,529</td><td class="num">₹1,29,759</td><td class="num">₹1,22,989</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>With NPS or UPS contribution of 10% of basic plus DA (Rs 11,035), a Class X employee at the entry cell would take home about <strong>Rs 1,25,494</strong> before CGHS, CGEGIS and any tax. Use the calculator below with your own cell and city.</p><Calc name="cgsalary" title="Level 11 salary calculator" intro="Move the cell to see how annual increments change gross pay. Rates are the current 7th CPC rates." preset={{"level": "11"}} />

<h2 id="scenarios">Level 11 salary under 8th CPC scenarios</h2>
<Figure name="level-11-salary-scenarios" /><p>The 8th Pay Commission has not announced a fitment factor, a pay matrix or a payment date. The table applies the four scenarios used across this site, plus the staff-side demand, to the entry cell and to cell 10, and rounds to the nearest Rs 100 as a matrix would.</p><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Fitment factor</th><th class="num">Entry-cell basic</th><th class="num">Rise over today's basic</th><th class="num">Gain over basic + DA today</th><th class="num">Basic at cell 10 (after 9 increments)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">1.92</th><td class="num">₹1,30,000</td><td class="num">+92%</td><td class="num">+17.8%</td><td class="num">₹1,69,700</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">2.28</th><td class="num">₹1,54,400</td><td class="num">+128%</td><td class="num">+39.9%</td><td class="num">₹2,01,600</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">2.57</th><td class="num">₹1,74,000</td><td class="num">+157%</td><td class="num">+57.7%</td><td class="num">₹2,27,200</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">2.86</th><td class="num">₹1,93,600</td><td class="num">+186%</td><td class="num">+75.4%</td><td class="num">₹2,52,800</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">3.83 (staff demand)</th><td class="num">₹2,59,300</td><td class="num">+283%</td><td class="num">+135.0%</td><td class="num">₹3,38,600</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>The last-but-one column is the one that matters. Today the same employee draws Rs 1,10,351 (basic plus 63% DA). A factor of 1.63 would only restore that total; the real gain is the part above it. At 2.28 the gain at Level 11 is about 40%, and at 1.92 about 18%. See <a href="/da-merger-8th-pay-commission/">DA merger</a> for why.</p>

<h2 id="progression">Level 11 pay matrix: first 10 cells</h2>
<p>Level 11 is the senior time scale for Group A officers, reached a few years after entry at Level 10. Entry pay is Rs 67,700 and the level has the same 3% annual increment pattern.</p><p>At this height of the matrix, a fitment factor produces large rupee gains even at the cautious end, while the percentage gain depends mostly on how much DA is merged.</p><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Cell</th><th class="num">Basic pay</th><th class="num">Increase over the cell before</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">1</th><td class="num">₹67,700</td><td class="num">-</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">2</th><td class="num">₹69,700</td><td class="num">+₹2,000</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">3</th><td class="num">₹71,800</td><td class="num">+₹2,100</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">4</th><td class="num">₹74,000</td><td class="num">+₹2,200</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">5</th><td class="num">₹76,200</td><td class="num">+₹2,200</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">6</th><td class="num">₹78,500</td><td class="num">+₹2,300</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">7</th><td class="num">₹80,900</td><td class="num">+₹2,400</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">8</th><td class="num">₹83,300</td><td class="num">+₹2,400</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">9</th><td class="num">₹85,800</td><td class="num">+₹2,500</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">10</th><td class="num">₹88,400</td><td class="num">+₹2,600</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Each cell is the one before it plus 3%, rounded to the nearest Rs 100, and the increment falls once a year. The full list of levels is in the <a href="/8th-pay-commission-pay-matrix/">pay matrix guide</a>, and you can look up any cell with the lookup tool there.</p>

<h2 id="promotion">What promotion or MACP is worth at Level 11</h2>
<p>On promotion, pay is fixed in the next level at the first cell that is at least one increment above the current pay. The same method is used when the <a href="/macp-scheme-explained/">MACP scheme</a> gives a financial upgrade after 10, 20 or 30 years without promotion.</p><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Case</th><th class="num">Pay now</th><th class="num">After one increment</th><th class="num">Fixed in Level 12 at</th><th class="num">Monthly gain in basic</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Promotion at cell 1</th><td class="num">₹67,700</td><td class="num">₹69,700</td><td class="num">₹78,800 (cell 1)</td><td class="num">₹11,100</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Promotion or MACP at cell 10 (about 9 years in the level)</th><td class="num">₹88,400</td><td class="num">₹91,100</td><td class="num">₹91,400 (cell 6)</td><td class="num">₹3,000</td></tr></tbody></table></div><ul><li>Level 10 entry pay: ₹56,100, which is ₹11,600 lower than Level 11.</li><li>Level 12 entry pay: ₹78,800, which is ₹11,100 higher than Level 11.</li></ul><p>Figures use the 7th CPC pay matrix as rebuilt from the 3% rule and are for illustration. Your department's promotion rules and the official matrix decide your actual pay.</p>

<h2 id="estimate">Estimate your own Level 11 salary under the 8th CPC</h2>
<Calc name="salary" title="8th Pay Commission salary at Level 11" intro="Choose a fitment scenario and city class. The level and entry basic are already set for Level 11." preset={{"level": "11", "basic": 67700}} /><p>See the same breakdown for other levels: <a href="/8th-pay-commission-level-1-salary/">Level 1</a>, <a href="/8th-pay-commission-level-3-salary/">Level 3</a>, <a href="/8th-pay-commission-level-5-salary/">Level 5</a>, <a href="/8th-pay-commission-level-6-salary/">Level 6</a>, <a href="/8th-pay-commission-level-7-salary/">Level 7</a>, <a href="/8th-pay-commission-level-8-salary/">Level 8</a>, <a href="/8th-pay-commission-level-9-salary/">Level 9</a>, <a href="/8th-pay-commission-level-10-salary/">Level 10</a>.</p>

